    "forensics": "The losing cluster is driven by two primary mechanisms: tight stop-loss whipsaws around the ~0.60% threshold during post-10:30 AM mean-reversion periods (Trades 1, 2, 3, 10), and afternoon volatility decay leading to EOD square-offs where transaction fees overwhelm flat price action (Trades 4, 8). Furthermore, repeated false breakout entries in TATASTEEL indicate that a 2.35x volume multiplier is insufficient to filter out retail-driven liquidity traps in high-beta metals.",
